        "text_tNNyqd": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Consumers are increasingly becoming concerned about sustainability, and as a result, companies are experiencing immense pressure to ensure their packaging and labeling solutions and practices are environmentally conscious. For instance, 68% of highly empowered consumers surveyed in a <a href=\"https://www.forbes.com/sites/forrester/2021/01/21/empowered-consumers-call-for-sustainability-transformation/?sh=5d9c46d22042\" target=\"_blank\">Forrester study</a> “plan to step up their efforts to identify brands that reduce environmental impact,” and 61% look for brands using energy-efficient labels when making purchase decisions.</p><p>Many companies have already begun exploring different sustainable packaging solutions, and using compostable labels has recently gained traction. These labels come with numerous environmental advantages and meet the demands of eco-conscious consumers.</p>",
            "text_size": "text-base"
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "heading_VKxnhT",
