    "image_with_text_RPHbWg": {
      "type": "image-with-text",
      "blocks": {
        "heading_iNLLfY": {
          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Understanding Compostable Labels",
            "highlight_style": "none",
            "highlight_font_style": "italic",
            "highlight_style_color": "",
            "highlight_text_color": "",
            "heading_size": "h2"
          }
        },
        "text_AbDDNd": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Compostable labels utilize organic materials, like cornstarch, potato starch, or sugarcane. They are designed to break down and turn into nutrients in a composting environment, returning to nature. Compostable labels are different from biodegradable labels, which may decompose but don’t provide the additional nutrients that compostable products do. After decomposition, compostable labels can act as a fertilizer to improve the health of the soil in the area.</p><h3>Benefits of Compostable Labels</h3><p>Below are some of the environmental advantages compostable labels offer:</p><ul><li><strong>Elimination of Forever Chemicals (PFAS):</strong> Per- and polyfluoroalkyl substances (PFAs) are harmful “forever chemicals” widely used in various industries for their water and grease-resistant properties. Compostable labels offer an eco-friendly alternative, eliminating PFAs and promoting a more sustainable approach to packaging.</li><li><strong>Minimizes Landfill Waste:</strong> Compostable labels break down into organic matter, helping reduce landfill waste.</li><li><strong>Reduces Greenhouse Gas Emissions:</strong> Unlike traditional labels, which emit substantial amounts of greenhouse gas into the environment, compostable shipping labels are made from renewable resources, reducing greenhouse gas emissions.</li><li><strong>Conserving Natural Resources:</strong> The use of renewable materials in compostable labels helps conserve the use of natural resources.</li><li><strong>Sustainable Packaging:</strong> Compostable labels are inherently sustainable due to the ability of their materials to decompose to natural elements or be recycled for further use.</li><li><strong>Enhancing Brand Reputation:</strong> As previously mentioned, a large majority of consumers prioritize buying from eco-conscious brands. Compostable labels are an easy step to improve your brand image and meet the consumer demand for eco-friendly products while complying with enhanced sustainability regulations.</li></ul>",
            "subtext_color": false
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "heading_iNLLfY",
        "text_AbDDNd"
      ],
